    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 15</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LVIIII. Se ðe hereteama<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-4"/> betygen sie, he hine be his wergilde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-4"/> áliese oððe be his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.3-2"/> were geswicne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LVIIII. Se ðe hereteame betigen sie, he hine be his weregilde aliese oððe be his were geswicne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LIX. Se ðe hereteame betogen sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-3"/>, he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-3"/> hine be his weregilde alyse oððe be his were geswicne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Be herge. Se ðe hereteama betogen sy, [he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.1"/>] hine be his wergylde alyse, oððe be his . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.2"/> g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>clænsie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui hereteama<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-2"/> (id est de conductione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-2"/> exercitus) fuerit accusatus, weregildo (id est natalis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.3"/> sui pretio)<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.4"/> se redimat uel secundum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_15.lnote.oe.5"/> weram suam neget.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be herge.] Se ðe hereteama betygen sie, he hine be his wergilde áliese oððe be his were geswicne<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_15.attnote.fn.9"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="380" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LVIIII} Se ðe hereteama betygen sie, he hine be his wergilde áliese oððe be his were geswicne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer [der Theilnahme an] Heerplündereien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15.lnote.de.1"/> bezichtigt ist, [je]der löse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15.lnote.de.2"/> sich aus durch sein Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_15.lnote.de.3"/> oder reinige sich [durch Eid] in Stärke seines Wergeldes.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_15.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever is accused [of taking part in] army-raids, let [each] redeem himself by his wergeld or clear himself [by oath] to the value of his wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>He who is accused of taking part in a raid shall redeem himself with his wergeld, or clear himself by [an oath equal in value to] his wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>He who is accused of [taking part in] the raid of any army is to redeem himself with his wergild or clear himself by [an oath of the amount of] his wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="381" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who is accused of taking part in a raid by a troop [of thieves], let him redeem himself with his wergild or clear himself by [an oath equal to] his wergild.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> were, <hi rend="italic">über</hi> his <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.:</hi> þam</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply were; above his, in the 16th cent.: þam</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Co Or;</hi> -mes <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> -mus <hi rend="italic">R M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Co Or; -mes T; -mus R M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nem <hi rend="italic">M Hk;</hi> -ctus <hi rend="italic">Brti;</hi> <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> de</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nem M Hk; -ctus Brti; without de</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pr. na. (uitalis <hi rend="italic">K</hi>) sui <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pr. na. (uitalis K) sui Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suo <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> (id — pretio) <hi rend="italic">App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">suo instead of (id — pretio) App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sic <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> sec. w. su. <hi rend="italic">App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic instead of sec. w. su. App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">herteama betogen sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">herteama betogen sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gyld alyse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gyld alyse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðam <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> his w. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðam instead of his w. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das <hi rend="italic">-a</hi> der Pluralendung, in Bu. H zu <hi rend="italic">-e</hi> vielleicht nur abgeschwächt, scheint als sg. von Q (instrum. <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>, gn. in Var. <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>, <hi rend="italic">-tiemcs</hi> Hs. Rs) und in Inst. als <hi rend="italic">heretema</hi> ‘Heerführer’ missverstanden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The <hi rend="italic">-a</hi> of the plural ending, in Bu. H perhaps merely weakened to <hi rend="italic">-e</hi>, seems to have been misunderstood as a sg. by Q (instrum. <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>, gen. in Var. <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>, <hi rend="italic">-tiemcs</hi> MS Rs) and in Inst. as <hi rend="italic">heretema</hi> ‘army leader’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst. übersetzen falsch, als läge ihnen doppelsinniges <hi rend="italic">forgielde</hi> vor, und missverstehen Wergeld des Verletzten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst. translate wrongly, as though they had before them an ambiguous <hi rend="italic">forgielde</hi>, and misunderstand it as the wergild of the injured party</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Den Stand des Verletzten berücksichtigt Ine hier nicht. Das Wergeld (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 30n) ist also Strafe, dem König zufallend; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 189. Busse für den Verletzten ist hinzuzudenken</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ine here takes no account of the rank of the injured party. The wergild (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 30n) is therefore a penalty, falling to the king; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 189. Compensation for the injured party is to be understood in addition</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Also 200 Eideshufen; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5. 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That is, 200 oath-hides; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5. 9</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_15.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>geswicne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geclensie</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 9 is printed 2 times on the page (14, 15), with one footnote.</note></note>
      </div>
